{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal, Anti-MRSA, Antibiofilm, Anticancer", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (96.43%) to Dermaseptin-DI2 A: 21%, L=K: 14%. Differing from AP00958 only at residue 9 (H vs. N). GRAVY: 0.164; mol wt: 2949.503; mol formula: C132H225N36O36S1; mol ex coeff: 5550. Activity: active against S. aureus ATCC 12600 MRSA ATCC BAA-1720 (MIC 4-8 uM), E. faecalis ATCC 29212 (MIC 32 uM), E. coli ATCC 11755 (MIC 8 uM), P. aeruginosa ATCC 27853 (MIC 16 uM), and C. albicans ATCC 10231 (MIC 4 uM). MBC are the same or 2-fold higher, indicating bactericidal. In addition, it inhibited formation of biofilms:bacteria (MBIC: 4-64 uM) and disrupted preformed biofilms at higher concentrations (MBEC: 32-128 uM against these bacteria. Der-PS4 also inhibted the proliferation of cancer cells. In vitro toxicity: horse RBC: HC50 ~128 uM. It started to show hemolysis at 16 uM. MOA:bacteria: Also MOA:fungi:C. albicans: membrane permeated. Structure: random coil in ammoniium acetate and helical in 50% TFE, PC/PG, or PE/PG vesicles (1:1).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "31426323", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Molecules. 2019 Aug 16;24(16):2974. doi: 10.3390/molecules24162974. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04623", "source_id": "AP04623", "source_numeric_id": "04623", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04623", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Evaluating the Bioactivity of a Novel Antimicrobial and Anticancer Peptide, Dermaseptin-PS4(Der-PS4), from the Skin Secretion of Phyllomedusa sauvagii.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
